oh so this chair is not very stable  we've used this chair in a project that  we called the other kind of sleep  paralysis inspired media installation  the experience the question was what is  called sleep paralysis this is something  that happens as you just just fall  asleep or just just wake up so your body  is paralyzed but your eyes can open and  you may start hallucinating in all the  different modalities could be visual  could be auditory could be tactile could  be pressure on your chest and one of the  most distinctive feelings that people  get is a feeling of presence of  something animal not necessarily human  in the room somehow watching them or  having an evil intention towards them so  we basically took a study that I did  before in a dream a nightmare laboratory  where we collected hundreds of  descriptions of the presence episodes  and we've tried to use the elements like  for example what kind of sounds the  people here some people describe  electrical buzzing some people describe  sounds of steps some people describe  furniture moving we create a little room  where we wanted people to have a feeling  of presence in the room wisdom so we  wanted to intentionally try to make them  comfortable at the same time and  destabilize them a little bit and then  ask them did they at some point feel  that somebody was there in the room  wisdom and in many occasions they would  localize like yes somebody was walking  behind me and sometimes they would tell  the whole story like I felt it was a  little boy you know gently step  what chair  you
 

